      "citations": null,
      "text": "This builds RMW from the value-weighted monthly section of the 6-portfolio ME/OP file. RMW is the average of the two high-OP portfolios (Small HiOP and Big HiOP) minus the average of the two low-OP portfolios (Small LoOP and Big LoOP). The script reads only the value-weighted monthly block, treats -99.99 and -999 as missing, and writes one row per month where all four returns are available.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef _norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r'[^a-z]', '', s.lower())\n\n\ndef main():\n    fname = '6_Portfolios_ME_OP_2x3.csv'\n    with open(fname, encoding='latin-1') as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the value-weighted monthly section\n    start = None\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        ll = l.lower()\n        if 'value' in ll and 'weighted' in ll and 'monthly' in ll:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        start = 0  # fallback: scan from top\n\n    # Locate header line (first subsequent line containing a comma and non-date names)\n    header_idx = None\n    for j in range(start, len(lines)):\n        l = lines[j].strip()\n        if ',' in l and not re.match(r'^\\s*\\d{6}\\s*,', l):\n            header_idx = j\n            break\n\n    col_idx = None\n    if header_idx is not None:\n        names = [h.strip() for h in lines[header_idx].split(',')][1:]\n        normed = [_norm(n) for n in names]\n        try:\n            col_idx = {\n                'sl': normed.index('smallloop'),\n                'sh': normed.index('smallhiop'),\n                'bl': normed.index('bigloop'),\n                'bh': normed.index('bighiop'),\n            }\n        except ValueError:\n            col_idx = None\n    if col_idx is None:\n        # Positional fallback: SMALL LoOP, ME1 OP2, SMALL HiOP, BIG LoOP, ME2 OP2, BIG HiOP\n        col_idx = {'sl': 0, 'sh': 2, 'bl': 3, 'bh': 5}\n\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    search_from = header_idx + 1 if header_idx is not None else start\n    for j in range(search_from, len(lines)):\n        raw = lines[j].strip()\n        if not raw:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in raw.split(',')]\n        if re.fullmatch(r'\\d{6}', parts[0]):\n            started = True\n            vals = []\n            for k in range(1, len(parts)):\n                try:\n                    v = float(parts[k])\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if v in (-99.99, -999.0):\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            # pad if short\n            while len(vals) < 6:\n                vals.append(np.nan)\n            rows.append([int(parts[0])] + vals)\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break\n\n    cols = ['date'] + [f'c{k}' for k in range(len(rows[0]) - 1)] if rows else ['date']\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=cols)\n\n    sl = df[f'c{col_idx[\"sl\"]}']\n    sh = df[f'c{col_idx[\"sh\"]}']\n    bl = df[f'c{col_idx[\"bl\"]}']\n    bh = df[f'c{col_idx[\"bh\"]}']\n\n    rmw = 0.5 * (sh + bh) - 0.5 * (sl + bl)\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame({'date': df['date'].astype(int), 'value': rmw})\n    out = out.dropna(subset=['value']).reset_index(drop=True)\n    out['date'] = out['date'].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv('output.csv', index=False, columns=['date', 'value'], float_format='%.6f')\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
